  "content": {
    "id": "p18-q18-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "18",
    "prompt": "Find all pairs of positive integers $(m,n)$ for which $mx^2+mnx+n=0$ has one solution.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$(m,n)=(1,4),(2,2),(4,1)$.\n\nSet $\\Delta=0$ to obtain $mn=4$, then list its positive-integer factor pairs.",
      "worked": "As $m>0$, the equation is quadratic. One real solution requires $\\Delta=0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Delta&=(mn)^2-4mn\\\\\\Delta&=mn(mn-4),\\\\mn(mn-4)&=0,\\\\mn&=4.\\end{align*}$$\nHere $mn>0$. The positive-integer factor pairs of $4$ give\n$$(m,n)=(1,4),(2,2),(4,1).$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 60
  },
